label memory_confession:
    scene hallway_dark
    with dissolve
    with fade
    show ethan at right
    with dissolve
    with fade
    p "I am not leaving until you tell me the truth."
    e "You do not know what you are asking."
    p "Then explain it to me."
    "Ethan looks towards the staircase."
    "He seems to be listening for something."
    e "When Lily disappeared, everybody blamed the house."
    e "Our parents thought that somehow, she had escaped."
    e "The police searched the grounds, the roads and the nearby forest."
    e "They never found anything."
    p "And do you still think that she is here?"
    e "I know that she is here."
    p "How?"
    e "Because I hear her cry every night."
    e "Sometimes she cries, sometimes she laughs."
    e "Sometimes, she calls me by names that nobody has used in years."
    p "What name?"
    e "Big brother."
    "His voice cracks slightly."
    e "At first, I thought that I was imagining it."
    e "Then I started hearing footsteps outside the bedroom."
    e "Every night, at exactly 3:17."
    p "Why did you not leave?"
    e "I tried."
    p "What do you mean?"
    e "I left this house while I was eighteen."
    e "I moved away, found work and tried to live a normal life."
    e "For a while, it worked."
    "He then rubs his face with both hands."
    e "Then suddenly, one night, I heard it... Three knocks on my apartment door.."
    e "When I opened it, there was nobody outside, but then i looked at the floor."
    e "It was a photograph of Lily..."
    p "The same photograph?"
    e "No."
    e "It was a new one.."
    "Ethan reaches out to his pocket and takes out a folded piece of paper."
    e "There was a message written in the back."
    p "And what did it say?"
    e "Come home."
    "You then hear another knock from upstairs."
    l "Ethan, I am lonely."
    "He closes his eyes."
    e "Every time I return, the house lets me leave again."
    e "But it always calls me back."
    p "Then we should just burn the place down."
    e "I tried that too."
    p "What?"
    e "The fire went out by itself."
    e "The house did not even get warm when I tried to burn it."
    e "You glance at the staircase leading to the door upstairs."
    "The darkness at the top seemed darker than before."
    p "What does it want from us."
    e "I do not know."
    e "But I think that it wants us to remember."
    p "Remember what?"
    e "What you did that Night."
    "A sharp pain spreads through your head."
    "Some images start flashing through your head, a staircase, a locked door, and a little girl's hands slipping away from yours."
    l "You promised."
    p "Stop it..."
    e "What do you see?"
    p "I... I locked the door."
    "Ethan goes completely still."
    e "You remember?"
    p "I did not mean to!"
    p "We were playing. She wanted to hide, and then I locked the door. I thought that it would be funny."
    p "I locked it from the outside."
    e "Then why did you not open it?"
    p "I heard her crying..."
    p "I thought that we would get in trouble."
    "Your hands begin to shake."
    p "I left her there..."
    e "And in the next morning?"
    p "I told everyone that I had not seen her."
    "Ethan turns away from you."
    e "I knew that you were hiding something."
    e "I just did not know if you remembered."
    p "I am sorry."
    e "You do not have to apologise to me."
    "A long silence follows."
    e "She is the one that you need to apologize to."
    e "You do not have to apologize to me."
    "A long silence follows."
    e "She is the one that you need to apologise to."
    scene upstairs_door at bg_fit
    with dissolve
    with fade
    "The door at the end of the hallway stands before you."
    "A faint light shines beneath it."
    l "I herd everything."
    "The doorknob turns."
    menu:
        "Open the door and face Lily.":
            $ opened_door = True
            jump door_decision
        "Leave the house with Ethan":
            jump ending_memory
        "Refuse to go to the door.":
            jump ending_escape
            
